  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">At head of title: "Premio América Bobia 2013."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Poem printed on brown paper which has border of animal silhouettes printed in black.  Preceding the poem, which begins on page 7, are three illustrated leaves: the first is printed on both sides with rows of animal silhouettes in black, with a large keyhole cut out in center; the second is the title page illustrated on recto with a black keyhole and key, and on the verso, with drawing of a group of animals in shape of a keyhole; the third leaf takes you through the keyhole to the world of "Zoológico" on a second title page bearing name of illustrator, and bordered along upper and lower edges with brown paper animal cutouts; colophon page at end decorated with cutout of publisher's lamp logo enhanced with orange, yellow, blue, and gold metallic acrylic paint.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Booklet issued in folder-style stiff paper cover covered with mottled green, orange, blue, and yellow cloth; collage on upper cover includes cutouts of three human figures with animal heads, ornamental panel with poet's name, and title letters mounted on a triangle of corrugated cardboard; wrapped around the three figures in center is a gold metal key on white string; lower cover decorated with cutouts of publisher's lamp logo, publisher's name, and series title; white lining papers printed with rows of animal silhouettes in black.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"...consta de doscientos ejemplares manufacturados e iluminados a mano por las Ediciones Vigía en su Colección Del San Juan. Para la realización fueron usados papeles y cartulinas de diferentes texturas y gramajes, colores acrílicos y textiles. Las llaves que aparecen en cada ejemplar fueron traídas por amigos y miembros del taller editorial"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
